        "target": "First, I calculate the earnings from the lower-paid work. Dan did 400 tasks at $0.25 each, so:\n400 tasks * $0.25/task = $100\n\nNext, I calculate the earnings from the higher-paid work. Dan did 5 tasks at $2.00 each, so:\n5 tasks * $2.00/task = $10\n\nTo find out how much more Dan made from the higher-paid work, I subtract the earnings from the lower-paid work from the earnings from the higher-paid work:\n$10 - $100 = -$90\n\nSince the result is negative, it means Dan actually made $90 less from the higher-paid work compared to the lower-paid work. However, the question asks how much more Dan made from the good work, which in this case is less, so the answer is $90 less, but the problem asks for \"how much more,\" which would be a negative value.\n\nFINAL: -90",
