        "target": "Given that Jerome runs the trail in 6 hours at a speed of 4 MPH, we can first calculate the distance of the trail. Distance is calculated as speed multiplied by time, so the distance is \\(4 \\text{ MPH} \\times 6 \\text{ hours} = 24 \\text{ miles}\\).\n\nNero runs the same 24-mile trail in 3 hours. To find Nero's speed, we use the formula speed = distance / time. Substituting the known values, Nero's speed is \\(24 \\text{ miles} / 3 \\text{ hours} = 8 \\text{ MPH}\\).\n\nFINAL: 8",
