        ],
        "student_prefix_sha256": "358850ed18e611972a41101c8e8889e68f590a4844460846fcf37a38937b16a6",
        "target": "Given:\n- Jerry's one-way trip to school takes 15 minutes.\n- The school is 4 miles away.\n- Jerry can run to the school and back in the time it takes Carson to run to the school.\n\nFirst, calculate Jerry's round trip time:\n- One-way trip: 15 minutes\n- Round trip: 15 minutes * 2 = 30 minutes\n\nConvert Jerry's round trip time to hours:\n- 30 minutes = 0.5 hours\n\nSince Jerry's round trip time equals Carson's one-way trip time:\n- Carson's one-way trip time to school is also 0.5 hours.\n\nNow, calculate Carson's speed:\n- Distance to school: 4 miles\n- Time to school: 0.5 hours\n- Speed = Distance / Time = 4 miles / 0.5 hours = 8 miles per hour\n\nFINAL: 8",
